note: >-
  No T2 or T1 doc changes in this WU, and that is the correct outcome rather than an omission: a
  design run decides how a screen will look and changes no user-observable contract, so UC-4 gains
  the controls when W6 builds them, not now. The rulebook is likewise untouched — run 10's Lexicon
  question was already written back at W5's distillation, so `export` has its row and this run
  consumes it (receipt verdict: inherited) instead of proposing a term. The two proposals the run
  does make are recorded in the run's own Proposals list and belong to their owners — the
  collection for Dialog, IconButton's TSDoc for the three glyphs — and neither is performed here,
  because a run proposes and an owner performs.
  One fact per tier held deliberately: the endpoint shapes live in src/api/routes.rs and are named
  in the run only by what the screen needs from them; the component contracts live in each
  component's TSDoc and the run cites @use/@avoid rather than restating states; and the run's own
  detail of which capability is used or deliberately unused lives in its capabilities table rather
  than being repeated in the Frame, which is why the Frame's Given line is a terse ·-separated
  list.
  Both new docs were snapshotted at creation and the epic plan before its first edit, so
  <doc>.html?diff=latest shows exactly what changed. verify-doc is green over every doc in the
  tree, with every relative href resolving on disk.
